{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# PRISMA 2020 flow diagram — ",
    {{ project_id | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Generated by command `llmexer analysis add-prisma`.\n",
    "\n",
    "| | |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| project | `",
    {{ project_id | tojson }},
    "` |\n",
    "| llmexer version | `",
    {{ package_version | tojson }},
    "` |\n",
    "| generated | `",
    {{ generated_at | tojson }},
    "` |\n",
    "\n",
    "Every number of the diagram is derived step by step below, with a note saying\n",
    "where it comes from, so the diagram can be checked and adapted. The logic lives\n",
    "in `prisma.py` next to this notebook - the same code `llmexer analysis draw-prisma`\n",
    "runs, reading and writing the same files. Numbers that cannot be derived show as\n",
    "`n = ?`; fill them in `OVERRIDES`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Inputs\n",
    "\n",
    "| variable | meaning |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| `SEARCHES` | search ids to count; empty means every search with results |\n",
    "| `SCREENING_DATA` / `SCREENING_DB` | `data.csv` and database of the title/abstract screening experiment |\n",
    "| `FIELD` / `LLM_VOTE_RULE` | yes/no answer field, and how disagreeing models are combined (`majority`, `any`, `all`) |\n",
    "| `PROMPTS` / `FULLTEXT_PROMPTS` | count only the answers of these prompts (screening / full text); empty means all |\n",
    "| `FILTER_PROVIDERS` / `FILTER_MODELS` / `FILTER_PROFILES` | count only the answers of these providers, models, profiles (both stages) |\n",
    "| `FULLTEXT_*` | the same for an optional full-text experiment, plus the field with the exclusion reason |\n",
    "| `COUNTS_FILE` / `SVG_FILE` / `DECISIONS_FILE` | the counts (settings, derived values, your overrides), the diagram, and the decisions per record |\n",
    "\n",
    "Paths are relative to the project folder. They were set when the notebook was\n",
    "created; change them by hand and re-run the cells.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from IPython.display import SVG, display\n",
    "\n",
    "ANALYSIS_DIR = Path.cwd()\n",
    "PROJECT_DIR = ANALYSIS_DIR.parent\n",
    "\n",
    "# `prisma` is the copy sitting next to this notebook\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, str(ANALYSIS_DIR))\n",
    "import prisma\n",
    "\n",
    "EXP_NAME = ",
    {{ exp_name | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "SEARCHES = ",
    {{ searches | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "SCREENING_DATA = ",
    {{ screening_data | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "SCREENING_DB = ",
    {{ screening_db | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "FIELD = ",
    {{ field | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "LLM_VOTE_RULE = ",
    {{ llm_vote_rule | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "PROMPTS = ",
    {{ prompts | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "FILTER_PROVIDERS = ",
    {{ filter_providers | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "FILTER_MODELS = ",
    {{ filter_models | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "FILTER_PROFILES = ",
    {{ filter_profiles | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "FULLTEXT_EXP = ",
    {{ fulltext_exp | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "FULLTEXT_DATA = ",
    {{ fulltext_data | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "FULLTEXT_DB = ",
    {{ fulltext_db | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "FULLTEXT_FIELD = ",
    {{ fulltext_field | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "FULLTEXT_PROMPTS = ",
    {{ fulltext_prompts | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "REASON_FIELD = ",
    {{ reason_field | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "TITLE = ",
    {{ title | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "COUNTS_FILE = ANALYSIS_DIR / ",
    {{ counts_file | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "SVG_FILE = ANALYSIS_DIR / ",
    {{ svg_file | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "DECISIONS_FILE = ANALYSIS_DIR / ",
    {{ decisions_file | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "LLMEXER_VERSION = ",
    {{ package_version | pyliteral | tojson }},
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def in_project(path):\n",
    "    return PROJECT_DIR / path if path else None\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Saved in COUNTS_FILE, so `llmexer analysis draw-prisma` re-uses them.\n",
    "SETTINGS = {\n",
    "    'exp': EXP_NAME,\n",
    "    'searches': SEARCHES,\n",
    "    'field': FIELD,\n",
    "    'llm_vote_rule': LLM_VOTE_RULE,\n",
    "    'prompt': PROMPTS,\n",
    "    'filter_provider': FILTER_PROVIDERS,\n",
    "    'filter_model': FILTER_MODELS,\n",
    "    'filter_profile': FILTER_PROFILES,\n",
    "    'fulltext_exp': FULLTEXT_EXP,\n",
    "    'fulltext_field': FULLTEXT_FIELD,\n",
    "    'fulltext_prompt': FULLTEXT_PROMPTS,\n",
    "    'reason_field': REASON_FIELD,\n",
    "    'title': TITLE,\n",
    "}\n",
    "INPUTS = {'llmexer_version': LLMEXER_VERSION}\n",
    "for key, path in [\n",
    "    ('screening_data', SCREENING_DATA),\n",
    "    ('screening_db', SCREENING_DB),\n",
    "    ('fulltext_data', FULLTEXT_DATA),\n",
    "    ('fulltext_db', FULLTEXT_DB),\n",
    "]:\n",
    "    if path:\n",
    "        INPUTS[key] = path\n",
    "\n",
    "searches = SEARCHES or prisma.list_searches(PROJECT_DIR)\n",
    "print(f'searches: {searches}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Identification\n",
    "\n",
    "Records found per database, duplicates removed (between the engines of one\n",
    "search, and between searches) and records dropped by `llmexer search filter`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if searches:\n",
    "    identified, note = prisma.identified_by_database(PROJECT_DIR, searches)\n",
    "    print(f'identified : {identified}\\n  ({note})')\n",
    "    duplicates, note = prisma.duplicates_removed(PROJECT_DIR, searches)\n",
    "    print(f'duplicates : {duplicates}\\n  ({note})')\n",
    "    automation, note = prisma.removed_by_automation(PROJECT_DIR, searches)\n",
    "    print(f'automation : {automation}\\n  ({note})')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('No search with a __results.csv yet.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Screening decisions\n",
    "\n",
    "One row per screened record: how many of the counted answers said yes / no /\n",
    "something unusable, the decision under `LLM_VOTE_RULE` (`llm_decision`), your\n",
    "manual decision from `DECISIONS_FILE` (`manual`) and the final `decision`.\n",
    "Records where the models disagree are shown separately - they are the ones worth\n",
    "a look by hand. To overrule the LLMs, write `yes` or `no` in the `manual` column\n",
    "of `DECISIONS_FILE` (and a `manual_reason` at the full-text stage).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "MANUAL = prisma.load_decisions_file(DECISIONS_FILE)\n",
    "print(f'{len(MANUAL)} manual decision(s) in {DECISIONS_FILE.name}')\n",
    "\n",
    "screening = None\n",
    "if FIELD and SCREENING_DB and in_project(SCREENING_DB).is_file():\n",
    "    screening, note = prisma.screen(\n",
    "        in_project(SCREENING_DATA),\n",
    "        in_project(SCREENING_DB),\n",
    "        FIELD,\n",
    "        LLM_VOTE_RULE,\n",
    "        filters=prisma.answer_filters(SETTINGS, prisma.STAGE_SCREENING),\n",
    "        manual=MANUAL,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    print(note)\n",
    "    print(screening['decision'].value_counts().to_string())\n",
    "    disagreements = screening[(screening['yes'] > 0) & (screening['no'] > 0)]\n",
    "    print(f'\\n{len(disagreements)} record(s) with disagreeing answers:')\n",
    "    display(disagreements)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('No FIELD or no screening database: the screening boxes stay empty unless set in OVERRIDES.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## All boxes\n",
    "\n",
    "The derived value of every box and where it comes from.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "derived, decisions = prisma.derive(\n",
    "    PROJECT_DIR,\n",
    "    searches=searches,\n",
    "    screening_data=in_project(SCREENING_DATA),\n",
    "    screening_db=in_project(SCREENING_DB),\n",
    "    field=FIELD,\n",
    "    rule=LLM_VOTE_RULE,\n",
    "    fulltext_data=in_project(FULLTEXT_DATA),\n",
    "    fulltext_db=in_project(FULLTEXT_DB),\n",
    "    fulltext_field=FULLTEXT_FIELD,\n",
    "    reason_field=REASON_FIELD,\n",
    "    screening_filters=prisma.answer_filters(SETTINGS, prisma.STAGE_SCREENING),\n",
    "    fulltext_filters=prisma.answer_filters(SETTINGS, prisma.STAGE_FULLTEXT),\n",
    "    manual=MANUAL,\n",
    ")\n",
    "pd.DataFrame(\n",
    "    [(prisma.BOXES[key], box['value'], box['source']) for key, box in derived.items()],\n",
    "    columns=['box', 'derived', 'source'],\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Overrides\n",
    "\n",
    "Start from the overrides saved in `COUNTS_FILE` (also used by\n",
    "`llmexer analysis draw-prisma`) and change what you need, e.g.\n",
    "`OVERRIDES['included'] = 42` or\n",
    "`OVERRIDES['excluded_reasons'] = {'Wrong population': 12, 'Wrong outcome': 7}`.\n",
    "Remove a key to go back to the derived value.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "_, OVERRIDES = prisma.load_counts_file(COUNTS_FILE)\n",
    "# OVERRIDES['included'] = 42\n",
    "\n",
    "values = prisma.effective_counts(derived, OVERRIDES)\n",
    "for warning in prisma.check_counts(values):\n",
    "    print(f'warning: {warning}')\n",
    "values"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Diagram\n",
    "\n",
    "Saves the counts (settings, derived values, overrides), the decisions per record\n",
    "and the SVG, then shows the diagram. A file whose content changes is first copied\n",
    "to `.backup/`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "backups = prisma.save_outputs(\n",
    "    COUNTS_FILE,\n",
    "    SVG_FILE,\n",
    "    derived,\n",
    "    OVERRIDES,\n",
    "    values,\n",
    "    TITLE,\n",
    "    settings=SETTINGS,\n",
    "    inputs=INPUTS,\n",
    "    decisions_path=DECISIONS_FILE,\n",
    "    decisions=decisions,\n",
    ")\n",
    "for backup in backups:\n",
    "    print(f'backed up: {backup}')\n",
    "print(f'written: {SVG_FILE}')\n",
    "display(SVG(prisma.render_svg(values, TITLE)))"
   ]
  }
 ],
